<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>VLANVerify Report — {{ report.generated_at }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --held: #1a7f37;
    --held-bg: #eafaf0;
    --violated: #b42318;
    --violated-bg: #fdecea;
    --warn: #b26a00;
    --warn-bg: #fff6e5;
    --inconclusive: #5a6472;
    --inconclusive-bg: #f1f2f4;
    --border: #d9dde2;
    --text: #1f2328;
    --muted: #57606a;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    color: var(--text);
    background: #fff;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 4rem 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
  header h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0; font-size: 1.8rem; }
  header p.tagline { margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0; color: var(--muted); }

  .meta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: #f6f8fa;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .meta dt { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  .meta dd { margin: 0; }

  .dry-run-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--warn-bg);
    color: var(--warn);
    border: 1px solid var(--warn);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .banner {
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .banner.critical { background: var(--violated-bg); border: 1px solid var(--violated); color: var(--violated); }
  .banner.clean { background: var(--held-bg); border: 1px solid var(--held); color: var(--held); }
  .banner ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; font-weight: 400; }

  .summary-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .card .num { font-size: 1.8rem; font-weight: 700; display: block; }
  .card .label { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .card.held { border-color: var(--held); }
  .card.held .num { color: var(--held); }
  .card.violated { border-color: var(--violated); }
  .card.violated .num { color: var(--violated); }
  .card.inconclusive { border-color: var(--inconclusive); }
  .card.inconclusive .num { color: var(--inconclusive); }

  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f8fa; font-size: 0.8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: var(--muted); }

  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .badge.HELD { background: var(--held-bg); color: var(--held); }
  .badge.VIOLATED { background: var(--violated-bg); color: var(--violated); }
  .badge.INCONCLUSIVE { background: var(--inconclusive-bg); color: var(--inconclusive); }

  tr.violated-row { background: var(--violated-bg); }
  tr.warn-row { background: var(--warn-bg); }

  .arrow { color: var(--muted); }

  details.tech { margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  details.tech summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  details.tech table { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.82rem; }
  details.tech th, details.tech td { padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; }
  code { background: #f1f2f4; padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85em; }

  footer { margin-top: 3rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <h1>VLANVerify Report</h1>
  <p class="tagline">VLAN network segmentation test results — plain-English summary for review or audit evidence.</p>
</header>

{% if report.dry_run %}
<div class="dry-run-badge">DRY RUN — no real network traffic was sent; results are simulated.</div>
{% endif %}

<dl class="meta">
  <div><dt>Scan date</dt><dd>{{ report.generated_at }}</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Probe device interface</dt><dd><code>{{ report.device_interface }}</code></dd></div>
  <div><dt>Policy file</dt><dd><code>{{ report.policy_path }}</code></dd></div>
  <div><dt>Policy file checksum (SHA-256)</dt><dd><code>{{ report.policy_hash }}</code></dd></div>
</dl>

{% if security_violations %}
<div class="banner critical">
  {{ security_violations|length }} critical finding{{ 's' if security_violations|length != 1 else '' }}: traffic that should have been blocked between VLANs was NOT blocked.
  <ul>
    {% for r in security_violations %}
    <li>'{{ r.from_vlan }}' could reach '{{ r.to_vlan }}' — this boundary is not enforced.</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="banner clean">No critical findings. Every rule that required traffic to be blocked between VLANs was confirmed blocked.</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="summary-cards">
  <div class="card"><span class="num">{{ total }}</span><span class="label">Rules tested</span></div>
  <div class="card held"><span class="num">{{ counts.HELD }}</span><span class="label">Held</span></div>
  <div class="card violated"><span class="num">{{ counts.VIOLATED }}</span><span class="label">Violated</span></div>
  <div class="card inconclusive"><span class="num">{{ counts.INCONCLUSIVE }}</span><span class="label">Inconclusive</span></div>
</div>

<h2>Test results</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Rule</th>
      <th>Expected</th>
      <th>Actual</th>
      <th>Verdict</th>
      <th>Explanation</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for r in report.rule_results %}
    <tr class="{{ 'violated-row' if r.is_security_violation else ('warn-row' if r.verdict == Verdict.VIOLATED else '') }}">
      <td>{{ r.from_vlan }} <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> {{ r.to_vlan }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.expect.value }}</td>
      <td>{{ 'reachable' if r.actual_reachable else 'blocked' }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge {{ r.verdict.value }}">{{ r.verdict.value }}</span></td>
      <td>
        {{ r.notes }}
        <details class="tech">
          <summary>Technical details</summary>
          <div>
            Target: <code>{{ r.target_ip or 'n/a' }}</code>
            {% if r.target_discovered %}(auto-discovered){% endif %}
            {% if r.ports_tested %} &middot; Ports tested: {{ r.ports_tested|join(', ') }}{% endif %}
          </div>
          {% if r.probes %}
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for p in r.probes %}
              <tr>
                <td>{{ 'ICMP ping' if p.kind == 'ping' else 'TCP port ' ~ p.port }}</td>
                <td>{{ p.outcome.value }}</td>
                <td>{{ p.detail }}</td>
              </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          {% endif %}
        </details>
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Probe device connectivity</h2>
<p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
  How the probe device obtained an address on each VLAN under test. A VLAN with no address at all could not be
  tested from — this is itself useful information for an audit (e.g. a VLAN with DHCP intentionally disabled).
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>VLAN</th><th>Sub-interface</th><th>Address method</th><th>Address</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {% for s in report.interface_statuses %}
    <tr class="{{ 'warn-row' if s.method.value == 'none' else '' }}">
      <td>{{ s.vlan_name }} (VLAN {{ s.vlan_id }})</td>
      <td><code>{{ s.ifname }}</code></td>
      <td>{{ s.method.value }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.address or '—' }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.error or '' }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<footer>
  Generated by VLANVerify. This report reflects network behaviour observed at the time of the scan only
  (point-in-time test, not continuous monitoring). Full policy file is fingerprinted above by SHA-256 checksum
  for evidence purposes.
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
